Redis: 4 standalone masters + Sentinel (not Cluster). Route `campaign_id` -> CRC32C slot -> shard. Each `EVALSHA` must hit one shard. Hash tag `{campaign_id}` on all campaign-scoped keys.

Reference: `docs/SHARDING.md`, `docs/TRADEOFFS.md`, `hot-path.mdc`.

## Static slot sharding

```
slot  = CRC32C(campaign_id) & 1023
shard = slot_table[slot]   // versioned snapshot, atomic.Value in Go, synced to edge Lua
```

Production: `StaticSlotSharder` only. Jump Hash = tests/benches. Edge parity mandatory (`edge-slot-map.lua`, `sharding_test.go`).

Resharding: operator-led copy -> fence -> epoch bump -> drain. Not Redis Cluster slot migration. `MIGRATION_FENCE_ENABLED` -> Lua error 11 on fenced slots.

## Shard roles

| Shard | Global (replicated via outbox) | Local (per master) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 0 | pub/sub `campaigns:update`, auth lockout, brand creatives, BPF sync source | ingress counters |
| 1..N | config, blacklists, fraud boosts, placement pauses (fan-out from 0) | budgets, dedup, streams, fcap |

Key catalog: `internal/domain/redis_key_catalog.go` for slot migration COPY/EXISTS.

Shard-0 outage: reroute via `campaign_routing` triplet when configured; else `503 shard_unavailable`. Control pub/sub SPOF until Sentinel promote. Tracker: `REDIS_SHARD0_OPTIONAL_STARTUP=1`, `CAMPAIGN_REPLICA_PATH`, `CAMPAIGN_UPDATE_BROKER_FALLBACK=1`.

## Lua script tiers

| Script | Tier | Role |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `budget-fast.lua` | B | Impression budget debit |
| `unified-filter.lua` | C | Fcap, pacing, TTC, placement blacklist, migration fence |
| `local-quota-refill.lua` | — | Local quanta chunk fetch |
| `local-quota-return.lua` | — | Crash reconciliation return |
| `budget-rollback.lua` | — | Undo debit on post-debit enqueue failure |

p99 < 10 ms per shard. IP rate limits at edge/XDP only — not in Lua.

When `SetDeferStreamToProducer(true)`: Lua stream key -> `fcap:ignored`; Go `StreamProducer`/`BrokerProducer` sole `XADD` writer.

## Stream producer and admission

- Per-shard bounded queue (50k); vtproto encode on hot path; background pipeline `XADD`.
- `STREAM_PRODUCER_ADMISSION_PCT` (default 85%): `TryReserve` before debit; 503 before spend when near full.
- Post-debit fail -> `budget-rollback.lua` (200 ms timeout) or local quanta refund.
- Metrics: `ad_stream_producer_queue_depth`, `ad_stream_producer_admission_rejected_total`, `ad_stream_producer_post_debit_rejected_total` (should stay ~0).

## Local quanta

`LOCAL_QUOTA_MODE=live`: refill chunks via Lua; debit in Go memory (~16 ns). Full-skip eliminates sync `EVALSHA` for eligible traffic. Eventual consistency on crash — refill/return scripts reconcile.

## Processor consumers

`cmd/processor` per shard:

- `{REDIS_GROUP_NAME}_pg` — Postgres settlement, `balance_ledger`.
- `{REDIS_GROUP_NAME}_ch` — ClickHouse telemetry batches.

Independent PEL per group; `XACK` after durable write. At-least-once: PG unique txn IDs; CH `ReplacingMergeTree`.

## pkg/broker (optional CH ingest)

Not a replacement for Redis budget Lua unless explicitly migrated.

- `CH_INGEST_SOURCE=broker`: mmap WAL segments; tracker `BrokerProducer` mirrors admission path.
- Cutover: shadow (`BROKER_SHADOW_MODE=1`) -> drain `_ch` PEL -> broker-primary. Rollback: Redis consumers while broker offsets on disk persist.
- Divergence metric: `ad_broker_ingest_divergence_high` must be quiet in shadow.

## Postgres

Settlement and budget authority. sqlc per service under `internal/<svc>/db/`.

- Invariant: `current_spend <= budget_limit` (+/-1 micro-unit in tests).
- Outbox: config mutations in same txn as domain write — never direct Redis from admin handlers.
- UDS on appliance: `DB_DSN` with `host=/run/ad-event-processor/postgresql`.

## ClickHouse

Analytics and IVT batch paths only — not hot ingest authority.

- Canonical DDL: `internal/clickhouse/migrate/00000_bootstrap_tables.sql`.
- Spool on CH down: `CH_SPOOL_DIR` mmap WAL; `RecoverSpool` on recovery.
- PII: `ip_hash`, `ua_hash`, `pii_salt_version` only (`pkg/piihash`).

## Circuit breakers

Per-shard `RedisBreaker`: `REDIS_BREAKER_FAIL_THRESHOLD=150` -> open -> `ErrRedisCircuitOpen` -> HTTP 503 fail closed.

## Transport

Redis UDS when co-located: auto-detect socket path in `redis_shards.go` / `redis_connect.go`. Bench: `scripts/perf/redis_uds_benchmark.sh`.

